1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,746
A glass of water.

2
00:00:01,746 --> 00:00:03,187
The air you breathe.

3
00:00:03,187 --> 00:00:05,479
A spoon of sugar stirred into tea.

4
00:00:05,879 --> 00:00:07,932
All three look smooth and even.

5
00:00:07,932 --> 00:00:11,020
But only one of them is
a single pure substance.

6
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:15,951
Diya fills her bottle at the college
water cooler, and remembers a question.

7
00:00:16,301 --> 00:00:18,278
Is air a compound, like water?

8
00:00:18,278 --> 00:00:20,211
Or a mixture, like sweet tea?

9
00:00:20,711 --> 00:00:25,000
By the end of this video, you will
sort any substance into its right box.

10
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:27,048
First, what is matter?

11
00:00:27,398 --> 00:00:30,896
Matter is anything that has
mass and takes up space.

12
00:00:30,896 --> 00:00:32,721
It comes in three states.

13
00:00:33,071 --> 00:00:35,621
A solid has a fixed shape and volume.

14
00:00:35,621 --> 00:00:38,774
Its particles sit close
and only shake in place.

15
00:00:39,174 --> 00:00:43,310
A liquid has a fixed volume, but
takes the shape of its container.

16
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:45,560
Its particles slide past each other.

17
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,287
A gas has neither.

18
00:00:47,287 --> 00:00:50,581
Its particles fly apart and
fill any space they get.

19
00:00:50,981 --> 00:00:55,538
Change the temperature or the pressure,
and one state turns into another.

20
00:00:55,538 --> 00:00:58,811
Ice melts into water, and
water boils into vapour.

21
00:00:59,461 --> 00:01:01,675
Now let's sort matter into boxes.

22
00:01:01,675 --> 00:01:05,180
Every sample is either a
mixture or a pure substance.

23
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:09,073
A mixture holds two or more
substances, in any ratio.

24
00:01:09,473 --> 00:01:14,010
If it is the same all through, like
sugar in water, it is homogeneous.

25
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:15,175
Homo means same.

26
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:20,585
If it is not the same everywhere, like
salt mixed with sugar, it is heterogeneous.

27
00:01:20,985 --> 00:01:24,278
A pure substance has only
one kind of particle.

28
00:01:24,278 --> 00:01:28,547
An element has only one kind
of atom, like copper or oxygen.

29
00:01:28,947 --> 00:01:33,948
A compound has atoms of different
elements, joined in a fixed ratio, like

30
00:01:33,948 --> 00:01:35,754
water or carbon dioxide.

31
00:01:36,404 --> 00:01:39,401
Let's look inside air
on our molecule bench.

32
00:01:39,751 --> 00:01:44,351
Dry air is about seventy eight percent
nitrogen and twenty one percent

33
00:01:44,351 --> 00:01:45,251
oxygen.

34
00:01:45,062 --> 00:01:49,047
The rest is mostly argon,
with a little carbon dioxide.

35
00:01:49,447 --> 00:01:52,474
Different molecules, just
moving around together.

36
00:01:52,474 --> 00:01:54,696
No bonds hold them to each other.

37
00:01:55,096 --> 00:01:56,599
Now look at water.

38
00:01:56,599 --> 00:01:58,654
Every particle is the same.

39
00:01:58,654 --> 00:02:01,876
Two hydrogen atoms bonded
to one oxygen atom.

40
00:02:02,276 --> 00:02:04,162
Watch how water is made.

41
00:02:04,162 --> 00:02:08,805
Hydrogen and oxygen molecules break
apart, and their electrons pair up

42
00:02:08,805 --> 00:02:09,969
in new bonds.

43
00:02:10,369 --> 00:02:13,417
The new substance is
nothing like its parts.

44
00:02:13,417 --> 00:02:15,341
Hydrogen burns with a pop.

45
00:02:15,341 --> 00:02:17,151
Oxygen helps things burn.

46
00:02:17,151 --> 00:02:18,971
But water puts out fire.

47
00:02:19,621 --> 00:02:24,729
On the counter: air has many kinds of
particles, in a ratio that can change.

48
00:02:24,729 --> 00:02:27,386
Water has one kind, in a fixed ratio.

49
00:02:27,786 --> 00:02:28,946
Pause and think.

50
00:02:28,946 --> 00:02:31,236
So is air a compound or a mixture?

51
00:02:34,436 --> 00:02:35,336
A mixture!

52
00:02:35,328 --> 00:02:40,032
Its gases are not bonded, the ratio
can change, and each gas keeps its

53
00:02:40,032 --> 00:02:41,180
own properties.

54
00:02:41,830 --> 00:02:44,959
Here is how to sort any
sample, one step at a time.

55
00:02:45,309 --> 00:02:46,209
Step one.

56
00:02:46,113 --> 00:02:48,744
Does it have only one kind of particle?

57
00:02:48,744 --> 00:02:50,618
If not, it is a mixture.

58
00:02:51,368 --> 00:02:52,268
Step two.

59
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:54,758
Is the mixture the same all through?

60
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:56,448
Then it is homogeneous.

61
00:02:56,448 --> 00:02:58,128
If not, heterogeneous.

62
00:02:58,878 --> 00:02:59,812
Step three.

63
00:02:59,812 --> 00:03:02,848
A pure substance with
just one kind of atom?

64
00:03:02,848 --> 00:03:04,523
Then it is an element.

65
00:03:05,273 --> 00:03:06,173
Step four.

66
00:03:06,166 --> 00:03:09,060
Different atoms, joined in a fixed ratio?

67
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:10,753
Then it is a compound.

68
00:03:11,503 --> 00:03:12,567
Remember this.

69
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,407
A mixture keeps its parts.

70
00:03:14,407 --> 00:03:16,496
A compound makes something new.

71
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,930
Now, one worked example.

72
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:20,866
Sort these six samples.

73
00:03:20,866 --> 00:03:25,975
Air, water, copper wire, sugar solution,
salt with sugar, and oxygen gas.

74
00:03:26,475 --> 00:03:29,229
Copper wire holds only copper atoms.

75
00:03:29,229 --> 00:03:30,129
Element.

76
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,509
Oxygen gas is O two.

77
00:03:32,509 --> 00:03:36,225
Both atoms are oxygen,
so it is also an element.

78
00:03:36,975 --> 00:03:40,996
Water holds hydrogen and
oxygen in a fixed ratio.

79
00:03:40,996 --> 00:03:41,939
Compound.

80
00:03:42,689 --> 00:03:45,898
Air and sugar solution
are the same all through.

81
00:03:45,898 --> 00:03:47,326
Homogeneous mixtures.

82
00:03:48,076 --> 00:03:50,491
Salt with sugar has separate grains.

83
00:03:50,491 --> 00:03:52,125
A heterogeneous mixture.

84
00:03:52,775 --> 00:03:55,511
A mixture can be split
by physical methods.

85
00:03:55,511 --> 00:03:56,926
Nothing new is made.

86
00:03:57,326 --> 00:04:01,286
Hand picking lifts out large
pieces, like stones from rice.

87
00:04:01,286 --> 00:04:05,296
Filtration holds back solids,
like tea leaves in a strainer.

88
00:04:05,696 --> 00:04:09,259
Crystallisation grows pure
crystals out of a solution.

89
00:04:09,259 --> 00:04:12,719
Distillation boils a liquid
and collects its vapour.

90
00:04:13,119 --> 00:04:15,446
A compound cannot be split this way.

91
00:04:15,446 --> 00:04:20,102
Its atoms are bonded, so it needs a
chemical method, like an electric current

92
00:04:20,102 --> 00:04:21,356
that splits water.

93
00:04:22,006 --> 00:04:23,471
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:04:23,821 --> 00:04:28,723
Some students call oxygen gas a
compound, because O two has two atoms.

95
00:04:29,123 --> 00:04:31,187
But both atoms are oxygen.

96
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:33,831
One kind of atom means an element.

97
00:04:33,831 --> 00:04:37,714
Hydrogen, nitrogen and oxygen
gases are all elements.

98
00:04:38,364 --> 00:04:39,812
Where is this asked?

99
00:04:39,812 --> 00:04:44,204
As short questions to classify a
sample, or true or false statements.

100
00:04:44,804 --> 00:04:45,982
Exam level now.

101
00:04:45,982 --> 00:04:50,657
Which set lists a homogeneous mixture,
a compound and an element, in that

102
00:04:50,657 --> 00:04:51,557
order?

103
00:04:51,267 --> 00:04:52,495
Pause and solve.

104
00:04:57,895 --> 00:04:59,270
The answer is A.

105
00:04:59,270 --> 00:05:00,953
Air, water, oxygen.

106
00:05:01,453 --> 00:05:03,574
Air is a homogeneous mixture.

107
00:05:03,574 --> 00:05:05,154
Water is a compound.

108
00:05:05,154 --> 00:05:09,099
Oxygen gas has one kind of
atom, so it is an element.

109
00:05:09,599 --> 00:05:12,768
B fails: salt with sugar is heterogeneous.

110
00:05:13,268 --> 00:05:15,887
C puts the element before the compound.

111
00:05:15,887 --> 00:05:20,515
D calls ozone a compound, but
ozone, O three, is still an element.

112
00:05:21,115 --> 00:05:22,576
Here is your recap.

113
00:05:22,576 --> 00:05:24,077
Screenshot this card.

114
00:05:27,277 --> 00:05:30,114
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

115
00:05:30,514 --> 00:05:31,414
One.

116
00:05:31,028 --> 00:05:33,838
Why is air a mixture and not a compound?

117
00:05:34,638 --> 00:05:35,538
Two.

118
00:05:35,174 --> 00:05:38,856
Is nitrogen gas, N two,
an element or a compound?

119
00:05:39,656 --> 00:05:40,556
Three.

120
00:05:40,226 --> 00:05:42,673
How would you separate sand from water?

121
00:05:43,573 --> 00:05:48,326
Next time: why does boiling water stay
water, but burning paper turns into

122
00:05:48,326 --> 00:05:49,226
ash?

123
00:05:48,838 --> 00:05:51,983
We find out in physical
and chemical properties.
